00:06:55.407 --> 00:06:57.397
"Why do I faint after blood exam?

00:06:57.397 --> 00:06:58.987
"The sight of blood doesn't bother me

00:06:58.987 --> 00:07:00.160
"and I'm not afraid of needles."

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:01.710
Farah, it sounds like what you're having

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.950
is called a vasovagal response.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.810
You, without even thinking about it,

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:08.286
your primitive brain
has a startling response

00:07:08.286 --> 00:07:10.551
to getting poked and losing some blood.

00:07:10.551 --> 00:07:13.087
It's not your frontal part of your brain

00:07:13.087 --> 00:07:16.541
which makes some of your more
complicated decisions for you,

00:07:16.541 --> 00:07:19.949
but your primitive brain starts
panicking that it saw blood,

00:07:19.949 --> 00:07:21.610
that you're losing blood.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.090
Your heart rate drops your blood pressure

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.170
and you don't get enough
blood flow to the brain

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.164
and when that happens,

00:07:27.164 --> 00:07:29.590
you faint or you feel
like you're going to faint

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:30.480
and you're gonna blackout.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.620
Not much you could do with that, about it,

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.880
but be cautious of standing up afterwards,

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.237
know that it could happen, and
take the proper precautions.

