00:08:03.637 --> 00:08:06.967
"Can you please make a video
on CT scans, MRIs, ultrasounds.

00:08:06.967 --> 00:08:08.667
"Are they really that dangerous to get?

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:11.188
"Can a CT scan actually lead to cancer?"

00:08:11.188 --> 00:08:13.679
MRI scans and ultrasounds are relatively

00:08:13.679 --> 00:08:15.739
benign Sanna, so you don't
have to worry about that.

00:08:15.739 --> 00:08:19.678
CT scans do pose a health risk

00:08:19.678 --> 00:08:24.280
because they do expose you
to unnecessary radiation.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.329
How much of that radiation
actually leads to cancer

00:08:27.329 --> 00:08:30.010
is a topic that's up for debate.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:32.570
I have talked to some
radiologists who believe

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.960
that the risk is overstated
because they believe

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:38.070
that the type of radiation
that you get from CT scans

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:41.155
is not the same type of
radiation that we've studied

00:08:41.155 --> 00:08:44.819
from Hiroshima and other times
when we use nuclear weapons,

00:08:44.819 --> 00:08:46.866
because that's what we
use as our basis of what

00:08:46.866 --> 00:08:49.370
is acceptable level of radiation

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:52.330
for the human body to
accept without health risks.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.740
If you don't need a CT scan, don't get it.

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:57.590
If there's a significant health
benefit for you getting a CT

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:00.221
scan like figuring out whether
or not you have appendicitis

00:09:00.221 --> 00:09:03.077
and you need emergency
surgery, yes, get the CT scan.

00:09:03.077 --> 00:09:04.840
But if your stomach
hurts and you just want

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:05.782
to figure out what's going on,

00:09:05.782 --> 00:09:07.424
maybe it's better to hangout a day or two

00:09:07.424 --> 00:09:10.740
and see if the stomach pain
goes away and not get a CT scan.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.800
Follow my logic there?

